# learning_service — Windsurf rules

Spring Boot 4 / Java 25 microservice that tracks user learning progress:
course enrollments, lesson completions, daily study activity, and earned
certificates. Three bounded contexts (`enrollment`, `certificate`,
`activity`) live side by side under `org.example.learning_service` and
must stay separated.

Always read `learning_service/AGENTS.md`, `learning_service/CLAUDE.md`,
and `learning_service/README.md` before editing.

## Rules

- Layering: `presentation -> application -> domain`. `infrastructure`
  implements ports defined in `application/ports/`. `domain/` has zero
  framework imports (no Spring, no `jakarta.persistence.*`, no Jackson).
- Aggregates own their state. `Enrollment` is the root for course
  progress; `LessonCompletion` is an entity inside it — mutate it through
  `Enrollment` (the `complete_lesson` interactor calls
  `Enrollment.addLessonCompletion(...)`), never via a standalone setter.
  `Certificate` is its own aggregate, 1:1 with a completed `Enrollment`.
  `UserStudyDay` is updated transactionally from the enrollment use
  cases, not from controllers.
- Ports for all I/O. Interactors depend only on
  `EnrollmentRepo`, `CertificateRepo`, `StudyActivityRepo`,
  `TransactionManager`, and domain services. Never inject Spring Data
  repositories or `EntityManager` into an interactor.
- Transactions go through `TransactionManager.inTransaction(...)`. Do
  not annotate interactors with `@Transactional`.
- Cross-context references are UUIDs only. No shared JPA entity, no
  shared schema, no synchronous lookup back to `course_service` or
  `user_service`.
- `application/certificate/CertificateStubS3Url` is a stub. To wire real
  S3, add a `CertificateStorage` port in `application/ports/` and an
  adapter in `infrastructure/adapters/`. Do not import the AWS SDK from
  an interactor.
- One use case per folder under
  `application/interactors/<aggregate>/<operation>/` and
  `presentation/http/v1/<aggregate>/<operation>/{dto,handlers}/`.
  Register interactors as `@Bean` in
  `setup/config_beans/<aggregate>/<Aggregate>BeansConfig.java`.
- Controllers return response DTOs mapped from `*View` records via
  `presentation/http/v1/mappers/<Aggregate>MapperQuery`. Do not return
  `Hibernate*` JPA entities or application views from a handler.
- Schema is owned by Liquibase under
  `deploy/liquibase/changelog/v.<version>/`. Hibernate runs in
  `validate` mode in production — do not regenerate the schema from
  entities.
- Build with Gradle Groovy DSL (`build.gradle`, not `build.gradle.kts`).

## Validation

Run from `learning_service/`:

```
./gradlew build
./gradlew check
./gradlew test
./gradlew bootRun
```

Tests use H2 in PostgreSQL compatibility mode via
`src/test/resources/application-test.yaml` (`ddl-auto: create-drop`).
Swagger UI at `http://localhost:8082/swagger-ui.html`.
